      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — clearer variable names, a descriptive test method name, and inline comments explaining the intent of each step.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version extracts the magic numbers into named constants (`EXPECTED_MJD`, `EXPECTED_NANO_OF_DAY`), renames variables to express their intent (`mockNow`, `utcNow`, `zeroDuration`, `utcAfterSubtract`), and gives the test method a descriptive name (`test_minusZeroDuration_returnsSameInstant`) — all while preserving the exact same method calls, arguments, and assertions."
